#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Pulmonary artery closed-surface repair / diagnostic pipeline.

Inputs from the clot-subtraction script:
  JL_Auto_ClotsSubtracted_ClosedBoolean.vtp
  JL_Auto_ClotsSubtracted_ClosedBoolean.vtp.facenames
  JL_subtraction_diagnostics/closed_boolean_cap_assignment.csv (optional)
  JL_subtraction_diagnostics/* (reference only; never blindly apply fixes)

Python >= 3.9; required: numpy, scipy, vtk. Optional: triangle, gmsh.
Works as a normal standalone script, not a ParaView Programmable Filter.

The operations are conservative by design:
  (1) Preserve input / export diagnostics early.
  (2) Remove duplicate/degenerate triangles only if topology does not worsen.
  (3) Identify vertex- vs edge-connected components; remove ONLY tiny detached
      components with no cap or inlet faces (and below an area bound).
  (4) Rebuild cap interiors with fixed wall/cap seams using constrained Triangle
      (when installed), otherwise VTK contour triangulation. Never shift a
      vessel-wall vertex. Each candidate is validated and can be rolled back.
  (5) Scan for nonadjacent intersections, including cap-wall collisions; report
      locations and associated caps. The scan has an explicit budget and never
      masquerades as an exhaustive certificate when incomplete.
  (6) Generate ParaView VTP markers and local patches for unresolved defects.
  (7) Optionally try Gmsh tetrahedralization with the original surface mesh;
      only then write a separate mesh-ready label if validation passes.

No code can infer the anatomical resolution of arbitrary overlapping surfaces.
Such defects are diagnosed but not automatically filled, deleted, or smoothed.
An unlabeled/missing cap cannot be confidently reconstructed by cap name.

CLI examples:
  python PA_Surface_Repair_and_Validation.py
  python PA_Surface_Repair_and_Validation.py --input JL_Auto_ClotsSubtracted_ClosedBoolean.vtp
  python PA_Surface_Repair_and_Validation.py --gmsh --full-intersection-scan
  python PA_Surface_Repair_and_Validation.py --no-cap-rebuild
"""

